  "behavior": [
    "The reconciler owns source selection and baseline enrichment. Pipeline acquisition, explicit observation publication, release imports, and runtime reconstruction call that entry point.",
    "Runtime reconstruction supplies stable change timestamps. It imports no acquisition pipeline or provider clients.",
    "CLI updates and the HTTP server share App.CatalogAcquisition. It applies the resolved provider binding set, credential resolver, and source directories.",
    "Omission preserves legacy provider selection. An explicit empty set makes no credential attempts and refuses a request for a provider outside that set.",
    "Two configured scopes make separate credential-resolution attempts. Construction makes none, and previews preserve the current catalog.",
    "The shared config accessor returns owned binding declarations and preserves explicit presence."
  ],
  "owner_decision": {
    "id": "D24",
    "decision": "Reset previous local acquisition while preserving the embedded or selected upstream baseline.",
    "current_cli": "starmap update --force",
    "go_option": "sync.WithFresh",
    "implementation": "pending manual runtime retention",
    "clarification": "The owner question used --fresh. The existing CLI flag is --force; no new flag or alias was introduced."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Manual acquisition still publishes through the root client without retaining original observations in the runtime input transaction.",
    "The current fresh pipeline still starts from an empty reconciliation baseline. D24 requires a behavior change before completion.",
    "CSP3 must retain manual observations, preserve source selection and previews, apply reset scopes transactionally, and prevent retired bindings from returning through local projections.",
    "CSP3 field presence, scoped deletion, and ingestion acceptance remain open. CSP4 authority, CSP5 collection, and CSP8 Starport adoption remain open.",
    "No latency or allocation claim follows from these catalog reconstruction checks.",
    "The full pre-publication repository gate, required code review, native qualification, and released-pair acceptance remain open. No push, merge on GitHub, release, or native CI dispatch occurred."
  ],
